Linux Troubleshooting Made Simple: find vs grep

📌 Suppose your web server is failing and you need to check logs.
Step 1: Locate the log file
You don’t know where the log file is.
👉 Use find:
      find /var/log -name "nginx*.log"
✅ It locates nginx-error.log.

Step 2: Search inside the log file
Now, you want to check only the error lines inside that file.
👉 Use grep:
      grep "critical" /var/log/nginx-error.log
✅ It shows all lines with the word “critical”.

📝 Summary
find = “Where is my file?” 📂
grep = “What’s inside my file?” 📜
They complement each other — often you find first, then grep inside.
